This assumes you believe that you can actually take ratios like that.
Myself I don't; I think units are *fundamentally* selbri rather than sumti
in Lojban, and that the natlang solution of thinking of quantities and
products/ratios thereof is actually quite strange, despite being
mathematically consistent. Under this standpoint only pi'ai/te'ai or a
similar system makes sense.

mi'e la latro'a mu'o

